"id": "lore-distill-a30",
"kind": "lore_distill",
"args": {
"topic": "Tantraloka 30 mantraugha: the multitude of Trika mantras",
"excerpts": "[sanskrit-trikashaivism TĀ 30 excerpts]\nChapter 30 = Mantraughaḥ / Mantrādi-prakāśana, 123 verses. \"Now the suitable multitude of Mantras (yathocita-mantra-kadambaka) associated with the processes of the Trikakula (trikakula-krama-yogi) is described, for the sake of those whose minds have not yet ascended to vimarśa, so they may accomplish it gradually.\"\nMonosyllabic mantras \"residing in Kula (kula-sthāḥ)\", \"giving siddhis through the Kula-krama procedure (kula-krama-vidhānena) and by means of subtle knowledge (sūkṣma-vijñāna-yogataḥ)\"; \"to be followed always by a woman or by a man\" — i.e. the Kula mantras are not restricted by sex.\nMantras \"without aṅga, without family (aṅga-abhijana-varjitāḥ)\" are to be worshipped by the best of adepts \"according to the single-hero procedure (eka-vīra-vidhānataḥ)\" — the deity without consort.\nLists: separate-seat worship (pṛthagāsana-pūjā) vs condensed worship (saṅkṣepa-pūjā) with mantra order; mantras ending in tālu (palate); Śrīmukuṭottara citations; Puruṣa/Prakṛti mantras; the twelve vowels (dvādaśa-svara) adorning bījas HRĪṂ KLĪṂ VLEṂ KLEṂ; \"visarjayet tāḥ prathamam anyathā chidrayanti\" — one should first discharge/dismiss them, otherwise they pierce (make holes).\n[TĀ structure] Ch.28 parvan/calendar + circle sacrifice; 29 secret Kula ritual (rahasyacaryā); 30 mantra multitude of the Trikakula (mantraugha); 31 maṇḍala construction; 32 mudrās.\n\n[Dupuche, Kula Ritual]\nThe supreme mantra of consciousness is SAUḤ, the supreme goddess Parā, expressing both the supreme reality and all that derives from it. The Kula ritual leads to mantra-vyāpti, the pervasion of the mantra; who knows this pervasion knows he is Bhairava. Chapter 29 is built on chapter 28. Six Kula sacrifices, each leading to a different aspect of the mantra. The practice is for \"the most advanced gurus and disciples\" (TĀ 29.2a).\n"
},
